From e62f3d1747cf763a0c94772d65f709a373d3398d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZeroScript <hipliteidk@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 06:45:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ZeroScript bridge: run out of the box against the on-device
 bridge

PrivateAgent speaks the OpenAI protocol, so it can use the ZeroScript bridge
(the free, keyless Roblox agent whose HTTP API runs on this device) - but three
things stopped it:

1. Cleartext HTTP. From API 28 on, plain http:// is refused at the socket
   level, and nothing in the manifest permitted it, so http://127.0.0.1:17614
   could be blocked outright. Added a network security config that permits
   cleartext for LOOPBACK ONLY (localhost / 127.0.0.1 / ::1); every other host
   keeps the platform default, so remote providers must still be HTTPS.
2. No usable defaults. Base URL and model now default to the bridge
   (http://127.0.0.1:17614/v1, 'zeroscript'), so a fresh install works as soon
   as the bridge is running. Existing installs keep their saved settings.
3. The API key was mandatory. The bridge ignores the Authorization header
   unless it was started with ZS_API_TOKEN, and there is no key to obtain, so
   the app refused to start. A loopback base URL now needs no key
   (isLoopbackBaseUrl); a real provider still requires one. isConfigured and
   every request guard follow the same rule.

UI: a ZeroScript preset chip in Settings and a ZeroScript provider card in
onboarding (pre-selected on a fresh install, key field hidden, and onboarding
may finish while the bridge is still stopped). Two tests cover the new rule.
Version 1.0.3+2022 so this build is distinguishable from upstream's.
